A||||9||fiero56||Another Record(for me)||||6||
Z||000000||fiero56||09-08-2000||11:42 AM||||Coming to you from the same guy who was able to remove the entire cradle/engine assembly from his '88 Formula in under 120 minutes, I just removed my entire dash in under 30 minutes. I pulled the Fiero into the garage at 11am today, and finished at 11:28am today. Today is the day I install my new 6x9 speakers in the 4x10 slots, without any dash modification. Hopefully the job will be completed sometime this afternoon.<P>Pictures will follow.||||reg||6
Z||000001||HugGRRRFiero||09-08-2000||11:59 AM||||A Torx screwdriver, 7mm & 10mm sockets, flat screwdriver (mainly for prying on electrical tab thingys) and your all set.  I love these cars!<P>Sounds cool, can't wait to see the pics.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||fiero56||09-08-2000||12:35 PM||||Yes, these cars are awsome. Everything is so easy to take apart. Only tool you left out is phillips screw driver, for taking the hood release mechanism off.<P>HVAC ducting modification is completed(took about 25 minutes). I brok one of my plywood speaker mounts in the process though. Will be cutting out another one soon.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||09-08-2000||12:56 PM||||All well and good but it still takes about 6 hrs. to clean it up for a show||||reg||1
Z||000004||87ECO5||09-08-2000||12:56 PM||||How fast do you think you could change out all of my old rubber bushings with fresh, poly ones!?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000005||Old Lar||09-08-2000||01:03 PM||||Maybe we could have a contest on how fast you can disassemble a Fiero and put it back together.  Best time wins the car.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||09-08-2000||02:16 PM||||One speaker mounted to the dash, one to go. I can't wait to hear what these things sound like inside the Fiero.<P>My thirty minute dash removal included time to bag and label the bolts I removed, and finding safe places for gauge pods, etc. I expect to be fished and have everything back in place by 4pm. We'll see if it happens or not.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Blade||09-08-2000||03:21 PM||||take some pics while your doing it id like to see what ya do to fit in the 6x9's...i bet they will rock.<P>Blade||||reg||1
Z||000008||87ECO5||09-09-2000||05:29 PM||||Well, I heard the results first hand last night and I've got to say they sound INCREDIBLE!!!!!<P>Drew, you did a great job!  They sound great, they've got solid mounting and you managed to keep the stock appearance.<P>Nice work, my friend!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000009||fiero56||09-10-2000||12:09 AM||||I wasn't too impressed with the sound quality on Friday, I think I was just too tired to really pay attention, and allergies took a little hearing away then also. Today I turned them up and they sound great. I can't believe the improvment. The sound is much cleaner, and sounds better. Bass response is a little better than 4x10, but not as much as I was hoping for. Maybe it will increase when I pick up a more powerfull head unit. I have an "old" one from dad's Sebring I am working on finding a wiring harness for. Will check Chrysler on Monday.||||reg||1
